# EAS Build project-archive excludes, at the REPO ROOT.
#
# EAS archives this monorepo from the root (its temp dir is named
# "<uuid>-shallow-clone" and contains apps/mobile/...), so an .easignore
# living in apps/mobile/ is never consulted — it has to be here.
#
# When this file exists, EAS uses ONLY these rules and does not merge with
# .gitignore, so everything that must stay out of the upload has to be
# listed here, not just the native folders.
#
# The specific failure this fixes: the tarball step died with
#   EBUSY: resource busy or locked, copyfile
#   '...\apps\mobile\android\.gradle\9.3.1\checksums\checksums.lock'
# because a local Gradle build was holding that file open. Nothing under
# android/ or ios/ belongs in the upload anyway — EAS regenerates the
# native project with prebuild.
#
# Patterns are intentionally UNANCHORED (no leading slash) so they match at
# any depth: "android/" catches both the retired Capacitor project at the
# repo root and the generated apps/mobile/android.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Generated native projects — recreated by prebuild on the build machine
android/
ios/

# Expo / build output
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local config — must never leave this machine
.env
.env*.local
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem
keystore.properties

# Local tooling / scratch
.claude/
.vscode/
supabase/.temp/
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
